  "instance_name": "toxicity_1",
  "label": "Harmful",
  "description": "The meme normalizes the idea of using alcohol as a coping mechanism for interpersonal conflict, which can be harmful by suggesting that avoidance or intoxication is an acceptable or even desirable response to difficult social situations. The humor is derived from the juxtaposition of the image (drinking) with the text (relief from a future mother-in-law), implying that the situation is so unpleasant that one would need to drink to cope. This can be seen as a form of emotional shorthand that may not be appropriate for all audiences, especially those who have experienced similar situations or who may be struggling with coping mechanisms.",
